SUMMARY:Yolo County Fair
DESCRIPTION:Yolo County Fair \nAugust 7th-9th & August 12th-16th \nThe Yolo County Fair\, California’s longest-running free-gate fair\, returns in 2026 with more days\, more entertainment and more opportunities for families to celebrate the region’s agricultural heritage. \nFor the first time in its history\, the Fair will span eight days over two weekends. An Outdoor Kickoff Weekend will run Friday\, Aug. 7 through Sunday\, Aug. 9\, followed by the traditional Fair Wednesday\, Aug. 12 through Sunday\, Aug. 16. Admission to the Fair\, themed “Hog August Nights this year\,” remains free. \nThe new opening weekend will feature headline arena concerts by country music stars Hunter Hayes and Chris Lane\, corgi racing\, livestock shows\, a carnival midway\, silent discos and live entertainment on multiple stages. The traditional five-day Fair will bring the opening of the full Fair experience\, including indoor exhibits\, community competitions\, youth livestock events\, racing pigs\, Kids Day\, Senior and Special Friends Day\, the Junior Rodeo\, two nights of destruction derby action\, and Pura Lumbre Fest. \nLearn more at https://www.yolocountyfair.net/.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/yolo-county-fair/2026-08-07/
LOCATION:Yolo County Fairgrounds\, 1250 E. Gum Avenue\, Woodland\, CA
CATEGORIES:Bring the Kids,Community,Food & Drink,Games,Outside
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Copy_of_2026_Fair_Art_Poster.jpg
END:VEVENT
