SUMMARY:Shades of Summer
DESCRIPTION:Seven Artists explore the nuance\, vibrant color\, and textures of the summer\nseason in a compelling new group show. \nThe Atelier is proud to present Shades of Summer\, a captivating visual arts\nexhibition showcasing works created by artists working out of Sacramento’s\nnewest studio hub\, the Atelier. \nThis month\, we welcome our visiting residents\, Celia Herrera Rodriguez\, Artist\, and\nCrisán Herrera\, Photographer\, to join us for our Summer exhibition\, bringing new\ncreative expressions to Sacramento. \nCelia Herrera Rodríguez (Xicana/O’dami) is a painter\, performance and\ninstallation artist whose work reflects a full generation of dialogue with Chicano\,\nNative American\, Pre-Columbian\, and Mexican thought. We are thrilled to have her\nat the Atelier this summer as she prepares for her museum retrospective. \nAlong with our resident artists\, Liz Awesome\, Betsy Gill\, Kenneth Jordan\, Jaime\nLuna\, and Izayjah McKinney\, they bring together diverse mediums\, from\nexpressive oil painting and mixed media to delicate textile art\, this exhibition\ninvites viewers to experience summer not merely as a calendar season\, but as an\nevocative spectrum of emotion\, intensity\, and atmosphere.\nSummer in Sacramento has its own distinct rhythm and palette\, Shades of Summer captures these fleeting moments through uniquely refined artistic perspectives. \nAll seven featured artists maintain active studio practices at the Atelier in Sacramento\, fostering a collaborative and inspiring dialogue that naturally translates onto the gallery walls. \nFeatured Artists:\n● Celia Herrera Rodriguez – https://celiahrodriguez.com/\n● Liz Awesome — https://lizawesome.art/\n● Izayjah McKinney —\nhttps://theateliersac.com/resident-artist-izayjah-mckinney/\n● Betsy Gill — https://www.betsygill.com/\n● Kenneth Jordan — https://www.kennethjordanart.com/\n● Jaime Luna — https://jaimelunastudio.com/\n● Crisán Herrera – https://www.facebook.com/crisan \nOpening Reception & Event Details:\n● Opening Reception: Saturday\, August 8\, 2026 | 5:30 PM – 8:00 PM\n● Exhibition Dates: August 8 – 25\, 2026\n● Location: The Atelier\, 2118 19th St.\, Sacramento\, CA\n● Admission: Free and open to the public; complimentary light refreshments\nserved \nAbout The Atelier:\nLocated in Midtown Sacramento\, The Atelier is a contemporary studio and gallery\ndedicated to empowering creators of all ages. Through a no-commission gallery\nmodel and process-led education\, the Atelier makes local art visible\, sustainable\,\nand accessible to all. For applications\, class schedules\, or to join the VIP mailing\nlist\, visit www.theateliersac.com or contact info@theateliersac.com.
